assess('A-NA','identity','Complete disodium selenite owner and negative source applicability','supported',[selenite],['E-NA-LINEAGE','E-CHECKS','E-ROWS','E-FIELDS'],
 'The exact56b2 owner remains CHEBI48843 disodium selenite. Official DSMZ863 actually prints Na2Se2O3 and MediaDive804 supplies no formula/CAS/ChEBI bridge; CHEBI48843 positively specifies one selenium per Na2SeO3 unit. The unsupported spelling inference must not resolve. REJECTED_LABEL preserves the exact raw literal and merge provenance without guessing a replacement reagent.',
 'All other aliases, including source-explicit Na2SeO3 (anhydrous), chemistry and genuine W01 source membership remain exact. CHEBI48843 capture corroborates CAS10102-18-8,2Na.O3Se,InChI and SMILES. Old CultureMech DIRECT_MATCH provenance and EXACT_MATCH grade are preserved; later label/CAS confirmation does not independently prove a new original matching method. Historical CAS source metadata remains attributable through its later correction event. Imported TRACE_ELEMENT and historical185 counts are retained, not newly approved. Native output drops only the unsafe Na2Se2O3 token plus truthful source-attribution change.')
assess('A-BORAX','identity','Conventional decahydrate and structural borax identity','supported',[borax],['E-BORAX','E-BORAX-TERM','E-BORAX-SUPPLIER','E-PARTONOMY','E-CHECKS','E-ROWS'],
 'The exact6f82 whole owner correctly preserves conventional sodium tetraborate decahydrate and CHEBI38888 structural borax. Primary crystallography explicitly equates the conventional name with Na2[B4O5(OH)4]·8H2O; atom totals are Na2B4H20O17, also Na2B4O7·10H2O. This is not substitution of an ordinary eight-water hydrate.',
 'CAS1303-96-4,formula,InChI/SMILES and all conventional decahydrate spellings remain consistent with that identity; supplier assay is not inherited as purity. Comparison with retained CHEBI86222 formula10H2O.H4B4O9.2Na/mass417.401 explains the earlier structural conflict. MANUAL_CURATION truthfully describes the representation adjudication while own-ID exactMatch stays unchanged. The broad MediaDive196 case remains unresolved for global redirect because DSMZ7700.1% stock is separate. All three exact UW child corrections are mandatory for standalone partonomy closure. BUFFER0.70 is a retained computational prediction, not evidence of approved role.')
assess('A-AS','identity','Empirical oxide input versus molecular depiction and alkaline stock','supported',[arsenic],['E-AS-TERM','E-AS-QUERY','E-AS-CCAP','E-CHECKS','E-ROWS'],
 'The exactaa045 whole owner denotes the As2O3 oxide reagent named by CCAP, not the NaOH-containing stock or arsenite generated in solution. CHEBI30621 explicitly defines arsenic:oxygen2:3, consistent with both empirical As2O3 and depicted As4O6. The actual OLS query and related synonym are retained, not falsely denied.',
 'The recorded final decision required representation adjudication, so MANUAL_CURATION is justified here; ordinary synonym verification is not automatically manual. The record deliberately adds no formula weight,CAS,polymorph,lot,vendor or functional role. CCAP quantity/stock hold remains separate. New evidence is LLM_SUGGESTION, history explicitly LLM-assisted, and source cases/occurrences are not rewritten.')
assess('A-SULFUR','identity','Whole four-origin elemental sulfur owner','supported',[sulfur],['E-SULFUR-SOURCES','E-ORIGINS','E-ISSUE368','E-CHECKS','E-ROWS','E-FIELDS'],
 'The exact77f915 whole owner consistently denotes weighable elemental sulfur CHEBI33403. The four authentic source proposals support the six case labels as powder/elemental-material names; they do not identify an atom, polysulfur-only polymer, sulfide ore, dissolved sulfide or a particular allotrope. MANUAL_CURATION records the preserved #368 material judgment.',
 'W01 DSMZ897/1092/854 prints5/3/10g powder separately from sulfide stocks. W05 TOGO2553/3129 prints5/20g powder. W06 frozen MMJS source explicitly names Elemental sulfer3g while its failed live requests are not positive primary retrieval. W07 DSMZ88 distinguishes0.5g powdered sulfur from20g sulfide ore; upper-case Powdered sulfur contexts retain TOGO2554 and archived DSM9463/9466 quantities with their own provenance. These quantity/process facts do not become universal owner properties. All four original proposal payloads, complete decisions, histories and aliases remain; rejected16S/sulfur atom/polysulfur/homopolymer cannot return. Metadata-only RAW_TEXT is already filtered natively. Empty chemical_properties avoids the removed atom/incorrectCAS claims. Existing habitat/role annotations and historical477 counts remain unapproved. Historical #368 canonical comment retention is a separate final-row decision; this owner review does not prescribe its loss or reuse.')
assess('A-DEFER','scope','Three installation deferrals without rewriting four source outcomes','supported',[defers],['E-DEFER','E-CHECKS','E-SEMANTICS'],
 'The exactd403 bridge is justified: preserve real nominal recipe evidence while deferring installation of the three proposed distinct owners. NBRC1020 leaves tungstate hydration unspecified whereas JCM317 explicitly supplies dihydrate; that omission proves neither sameness nor difference. NBRC1257/1321 bicarbonate names8.4g plus100mL water/CO2/sealed autoclaving; comparison with J45184g/L underCO2 does not establish a distinct stock identity.',
 'No inferred anhydrous form, final volume, common owner, rejection of supported recipe facts, source-case deletion or alias-based retarget is authorized. All three exact original operations and four complete decision objects are retained. The genuine generic84g/L edit remains separate. Native full1879 accounting/crosswalk and fresh root acceptance are later construction obligations; this report does not produce a future plan hash.')
